「リテラシーを身につけて成長するまで、スマホを持たせてはいけない」って思わしたっぽい
"...learns media literacy and matures, we can't let her have a smartphone." That's what they thought.

132
00:09:04,233 --> 00:09:05,033
うん
Yeah.

133
00:09:05,233 --> 00:09:08,533
そう、反動で今ドパマンダーになってるのじゃ
Yeah, and from the rebound, I've become a "Dopamander" now!

134
00:09:09,033 --> 00:09:11,233
ド反動ですのじゃ
A total rebound!

135
00:09:12,033 --> 00:09:12,833
当時...
Back then...

136
00:09:13,133 --> 00:09:20,933
え、そう、だからさ、結構さ、ニコニコ動画とかその古のインターネットミームとか
Yeah, so like, Nico Nico Douga or ancient internet memes...

137
00:09:21,333 --> 00:09:27,133
そのわしが禁止されてた時期に流行った、あの
the stuff that was trending during the time I was banned from the internet...

138
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:33,033
コンテンツみたいなのを知ってる人が羨ましいのじゃ
I'm really envious of people who know about that content!

139
00:09:33,133 --> 00:09:35,833
わしその時期触れなかったから
Because I couldn't touch the internet during that time.

140
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:36,833
うん
Yeah.

141
00:09:37,033 --> 00:09:41,833
反動というのは、誰にでも訪れますのじゃ
A rebound comes for everyone.

142
00:09:42,033 --> 00:09:44,833
「友達と話合わなくならなかった？」
"Didn't you stop fitting in with your friends' talks?"

143
00:09:45,033 --> 00:09:47,833
えぇぇ...？
Ehhh...?

144
00:09:49,833 --> 00:09:52,033
友だち...？
Friends...?

145
00:09:54,033 --> 00:09:55,833
のじゃあ...
Well now...

146
00:09:56,433 --> 00:09:58,833
え、ど...なんか...
Uh, what... like...

147
00:09:59,033 --> 00:10:00,033
そう...
Well...

148
00:10:00,045 --> 00:10:01,345
そんな、その...
Like, back then...

149
00:10:01,345 --> 00:10:05,545
そんな、その時めっちゃ仲いい子がいなかった...
I didn't really have anyone I was super close with...

150
00:10:06,845 --> 00:10:09,545
その... 要はその、わしが...
Like... Basically, back when I...

151
00:10:09,545 --> 00:10:13,545
あの、キッズフィルタリングみたいなされてた頃は、やっぱ...
...was under that kids filtering restriction thing, you know...

152
00:10:13,545 --> 00:10:15,245
人間低学年、だ、しょ...
When I was in lower human grades—like, ele—

153
00:10:15,245 --> 00:10:18,845
人間で言うところの、小学生とか中学生の頃じゃろう？
...in human terms, elementary or middle school age, right?

154
00:10:19,045 --> 00:10:21,845
え、その頃って結構、なんか...
And back then, you know...

155
00:10:21,845 --> 00:10:24,545
見た目で迫害みたいなあったから。
...there was kind of persecution based on looks,

156
00:10:24,545 --> 00:10:27,045
角とか尻尾とか生えてたし、わし。
'cause I had horns and a tail growing out and all.

157
00:10:27,245 --> 00:10:30,545
なんか、あんまり馴染めなかった記憶...
I remember not really fitting in back then...

158
00:10:30,845 --> 00:10:33,845
た、楽しいゲームするか！楽しいゲームするのじゃ！
L-Let's play a fun game! Let's play a fun game!

159
00:10:33,845 --> 00:10:37,545
す、スパゲッティの、アットホームな、アットホームなスパゲッティのゲーム...
A s-spaghetti... homey... A homey spaghetti game...

160
00:10:37,545 --> 00:10:41,045
アットホームなスパゲッティのゲームするのじゃ。
I'm gonna play a homey spaghetti game!

161
00:10:41,045 --> 00:10:43,845
うん、のじゃ。うん。
Yeah, that's right. Yep.

162
00:10:44,245 --> 00:10:47,045
なんか、うん、そ、そうなのじゃ。
Yeah... Y-Yeah, that's right.

163
00:10:47,045 --> 00:10:49,045
よいしょ、よいしょ。
All right, all right.

164
00:10:49,045 --> 00:10:52,045
パスタ冷めちゃう？ええっと...
The pasta will get cold? Um...

165
00:10:52,545 --> 00:10:55,545
ええっと、ちょっと待つのじゃ。
Um, hold on a second.

166
00:10:55,845 --> 00:10:56,845
うん。
Yeah.

167
00:10:56,845 --> 00:10:59,845
あ、でもでもでも！補足、補足！1点補足！
Ah, but wait, wait, wait! One point of clarification!

168
00:10:59,845 --> 00:11:00,845
でも、あの...
But, um...

169
00:11:00,845 --> 00:11:05,245
わしが人間に擬態する術を身につけてからは、
...after I learned the art of disguising myself as a human,

170
00:11:05,245 --> 00:11:08,845
あの、友達とかもでき始めたし、から、
I started making friends and all, so...

171
00:11:08,845 --> 00:11:13,545
あの、安心してほしいのじゃ。うん、安心してほしいのじゃ。
...I want you not to worry! Yeah, don't worry about me.

172
00:11:14,045 --> 00:11:18,045
パスタ、パスタ食べる。パスタ食べる。ええっとね...
Pasta, gonna eat pasta. Gonna eat pasta. Um...

173
00:11:18,545 --> 00:11:21,545
そう、どうやらアットホームな...
Right, so apparently it's a homey...

174
00:11:21,545 --> 00:11:24,245
アットホームなスパゲッティってなんじゃ？
What even is "homey spaghetti"?

175
00:11:25,545 --> 00:11:27,845
アットホームなスパゲッティらしい。
Apparently it's homey spaghetti.

176
00:11:28,045 --> 00:11:30,545
アットホームなスパゲッティ...
Homey spaghetti...

177
00:11:30,845 --> 00:11:33,845
「初心者でも安心」安心ってなんじゃ？
"Safe for beginners"—what does that even mean?

178
00:11:34,045 --> 00:11:37,845
あんまりその、スパゲッティを形容する言葉として...
As words to describe spaghetti, that's not really...

179
00:11:38,045 --> 00:11:42,245
初心者でも、ま、「初心者でも安心」はゲームに対してかな？
Well, maybe "safe for beginners" refers to the game?

180
00:11:42,545 --> 00:11:46,045
ゲームに対しての形容する言葉なのかな。
Is it describing the game?

181
00:11:46,245 --> 00:11:48,245
アットホーム言わない。
You don't call it "homey."

182
00:11:49,045 --> 00:11:51,245
言わない気がする。
I don't think people say that.

183
00:11:51,545 --> 00:11:56,045
から、なんじゃろ？フブキ先輩ミームが使いたかったのかな？
So... did Fubuki-senpai just want to use a meme?

184
00:11:56,045 --> 00:12:00,545
わしその、コマンドミーム？知らないから...
I don't really know command memes and stuff, so...

185
00:12:00,545 --> 00:12:05,545
なんか、「初心者でも安心」「アットホームな」みたいなのも、ミームの言葉なのかな？
Is stuff like "safe for beginners" and "homey" also part of the meme?

186
00:12:05,545 --> 00:12:09,545
そこまで含めて構文みたいな感じなのかな？
Is the whole phrasing part of the copypasta template?

187
00:12:09,545 --> 00:12:14,545
ごめんね、ミームの元ネタが知らないからさ。どこまでがミームのあれなのかわかんなくて。
Sorry, I don't know the original meme, so I can't tell where the meme ends.

188
00:12:14,545 --> 00:12:16,545
ふんふんふん。
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

189
00:12:17,045 --> 00:12:21,245
でもわし、わしの知ってる人間豆知識披露していい？
But hey, can I share some human trivia that I know?

190
00:12:21,545 --> 00:12:24,045
わしの知ってる人間豆知識なんだけど、
It's some trivia about humans that I know, but...

191
00:12:24,045 --> 00:12:27,545
あの、人間の、職場？
...in human workplaces?

192
00:12:27,545 --> 00:12:30,845
なんか、仕事？雇用？
Like, jobs? Employment?

193
00:12:30,845 --> 00:12:34,545
雇用募集みたいなので「アットホーム」って言葉が...
When job recruitment ads use the word "homey"...

194
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:38,845
書かれてるのは、アットホームじゃないってのを聞いたのじゃ。
...I heard it actually means it's not homey at all!

195
00:12:38,845 --> 00:12:41,045
それだけ知ってるのじゃ。
That's all I know about it.

196
00:12:41,045 --> 00:12:45,545
人間が使う「アットホーム」って言葉は、なんかすごい空気が悪いらしい...
When humans say "homey," the atmosphere is apparently super toxic...

197
00:12:45,545 --> 00:12:48,545
...との噂。
...or so the rumor goes.

198
00:12:49,545 --> 00:12:54,045
わしが人間と関わってる間に身につけた豆知識。
That's trivia I picked up while interacting with humans.

199
00:12:54,545 --> 00:12:57,045
「ということは」って何？
What do you mean by "which means..."?

200
00:12:57,045 --> 00:13:00,545
空気悪いの？このスパゲッティ。人間関係とかある感じ？
Is the vibe toxic? In this spaghetti? Like workplace drama?

201
00:13:00,545 --> 00:13:04,545
このゲーム、このゲーム人間関係あるのじゃ？
Does this game have human relationships drama?!

202
00:13:05,545 --> 00:13:07,545
ん？
Hm?

203
00:13:07,845 --> 00:13:10,045
対人ゲーか？
Is it a PvP game?

204
00:13:10,045 --> 00:13:12,545
対人ゲーか？
A PvP game?

205
00:13:12,545 --> 00:13:14,545
うん。
Yeah.

206
00:13:14,545 --> 00:13:17,545
でもなんか、やっぱ、新人に...
But really, giving a game...

207
00:13:17,545 --> 00:13:21,045
新人にさ、ゲームくれるフブキ先輩めっちゃ優しいですのじゃ。
...giving a game to a newcomer, Fubuki-senpai is so incredibly kind!

208
00:13:21,045 --> 00:13:25,545
めっちゃ優しいのじゃ。から、あの、嬉しい、ありがとうございますって思うのじゃ。
She's so kind! So I'm just so happy and grateful to her.

209
00:13:25,545 --> 00:13:30,045
あと、おかゆ先輩にもね、あの、ゲームをね、いただいていてね。
Also, Okayu-senpai gifted me a game too!

210
00:13:30,045 --> 00:13:33,245
あの、たんぽぽのやつとか、いただいてるから、
Like that dandelion one she gave me,

211
00:13:33,245 --> 00:13:36,545
それもまたやりたいなって思ってますのじゃ。
so I'd love to play that one again sometime too.

212
00:13:36,545 --> 00:13:39,045
先輩優しいのじゃ。
My senpai are so sweet.

213
00:13:39,045 --> 00:13:43,545
まだ、わし新人じゃし、あんまりお話もしたことないのに...
I'm still a newcomer and haven't talked to them much...

214
00:13:43,545 --> 00:13:47,045
ゲーム送ってくれるなんて。
...yet they sent me games.

215
00:13:47,045 --> 00:13:51,545
え、だってゲームって結構好きな人にしか送らないよね？
I mean, you only gift games to people you really like, right?

216
00:13:51,545 --> 00:13:54,045
え、じゃない？なんか...
Right? Isn't that so?

217
00:13:54,045 --> 00:13:58,045
結構ゲームを送るってことは親密度さ、高めなんじゃない？
Gifting a game must mean our bond is pretty close, isn't it?

218
00:13:58,045 --> 00:14:00,545
高めなんじゃない？
Pretty close, right?

219
00:14:00,545 --> 00:14:04,545
あの、お近づきの印的にさ、
Like, as a token of getting closer,

220
00:14:04,545 --> 00:14:09,545
なんか、仲良くなりたいって思ってるんじゃない？わしと！ねえ？
doesn't it mean they want to be good friends with me?! Right?

221
00:14:09,545 --> 00:14:13,545
え、だからすごい、すごい嬉しくて！そう！
So I'm just so, so happy! Yeah!

222
00:14:13,545 --> 00:14:16,845
すごい連絡いただいたときはめちゃくちゃ嬉しくて。
When they messaged me, I was overwhelmingly happy.

223
00:14:16,845 --> 00:14:18,845
楽しみなのじゃー！
I'm so excited!

224
00:14:18,845 --> 00:14:21,045
嬉しいのじゃー！
I'm so happy!

225
00:14:21,045 --> 00:14:24,045
じゃあ、ゲームやるお部屋に行こうかの。
All right, shall we head over to the game screen?

226
00:14:24,045 --> 00:14:26,545
よいしょ。
Up we go.

227
00:14:26,545 --> 00:14:28,545
よいしょー！
Here we go!

228
00:14:28,545 --> 00:14:31,045
のちゃー！
Nochaa!

229
00:14:31,045 --> 00:14:33,245
ん。
Mm.

230
00:14:33,245 --> 00:14:35,045
よ。
Yo.

231
00:14:35,045 --> 00:14:37,045
よいしょ。
All right.

232
00:14:37,045 --> 00:14:41,545
音量、どれくらいがいいんかの？
Wonder what volume level is good?

233
00:14:41,845 --> 00:14:45,545
ちょっとした音しか入ってないけど。
There are only faint sounds right now, but...

234
00:14:46,545 --> 00:14:49,045
音量もうちょい上げるか。
Maybe turn up the volume a bit more.

235
00:14:49,045 --> 00:14:52,045
オーディオボリューム...
Audio volume...

236
00:14:52,545 --> 00:14:55,045
これぐらいにしとくか。
Let's leave it around here.

237
00:14:55,045 --> 00:14:58,045
これぐらいでいい？
Is this good?

238
00:14:58,045 --> 00:15:00,045
ちっちゃい？
Is it too low?

239
00:15:00,657 --> 00:15:01,757
まだちっちゃい？
Is it still quiet?

240
00:15:03,557 --> 00:15:04,857
どうかのう
I wonder...

241
00:15:05,157 --> 00:15:06,957
開始してみないと分からん、ま、確かに。
You can't tell until we start. Yeah, that's true.

242
00:15:07,157 --> 00:15:09,157
割とこのちっちゃめの音じゃとね
With this kind of quiet sound,

243
00:15:09,357 --> 00:15:10,857
あんま分かんないよね。
you can't really tell.

244
00:15:10,957 --> 00:15:11,857
よいしょ。
Alright.

245
00:15:12,157 --> 00:15:13,057
よいしょ。
Here we go.

246
00:15:13,857 --> 00:15:14,857
いい感じ？
Good now?

247
00:15:15,557 --> 00:15:17,057
え、でもさ、わしなんかさ、
Wait, but you know...

248
00:15:17,057 --> 00:15:19,457
この、このなんか、これ気になってて
I've been kind of curious about this...

249
00:15:19,557 --> 00:15:20,857
何？これ。
What is this?

250
00:15:23,557 --> 00:15:26,757
ちょっと画面ちっちゃいの使っとるから、あんま見えないんじゃけど、
I'm using a small screen so I can't really see it, but...

251
00:15:26,857 --> 00:15:28,157
目が赤い。
Its eyes are red.

252
00:15:28,857 --> 00:15:30,557
目が赤いのがおる。
There's something with red eyes.

253
00:15:30,857 --> 00:15:31,757
何？
What is it?

254
00:15:31,757 --> 00:15:33,057
これはまた別？
Is this something else?

255
00:15:33,157 --> 00:15:34,357
映画とか？
Like a movie?

256
00:15:34,657 --> 00:15:35,857
なんじゃろう？
I wonder what it is.

257
00:15:36,457 --> 00:15:37,957
謎なんのじゃ。
It's a mystery.

258
00:15:39,857 --> 00:15:40,857
広告？
An ad?

259
00:15:41,057 --> 00:15:42,557
広告的なあれか。
Ah, an advertisement?

260
00:15:42,557 --> 00:15:44,557
広告だからあんま気にしなくていいか。
Since it's an ad, I guess I don't need to worry.

261
00:15:45,357 --> 00:15:46,457
よし、じゃあ
Alright then,

262
00:15:46,557 --> 00:15:48,057
一旦PLAYを
let's try clicking

263
00:15:48,257 --> 00:15:49,857
押してみますのじゃ。
"PLAY" first.

264
00:15:50,057 --> 00:15:50,857
よいしょ。
Here goes.

265
00:15:52,257 --> 00:15:53,357
ふむふむ。
Mm-hmm.

266
00:15:54,157 --> 00:15:54,957
手？
Hands?

267
00:15:55,157 --> 00:15:56,857
手と、部屋かな？
Hands and... a room?

268
00:15:57,057 --> 00:15:58,057
キッチンだ！
It's a kitchen!

269
00:15:58,357 --> 00:16:00,557
キッチンにおりますのじゃ。広い！
I'm in a kitchen! It's so big!

270
00:16:00,757 --> 00:16:02,057
え、暗い...
Whoa, it's dark...

271
00:16:02,957 --> 00:16:04,957
広くて高め、
It's spacious and expensive-looking...

272
00:16:05,557 --> 00:16:07,457
贅沢めのお家。
A fancy house.

273
00:16:07,657 --> 00:16:12,857
贅沢めのお家。Look at the Spaghet to see the Slap Sequence.
A fancy house. "Look at the Spaghet to see the Slap Sequence."

274
00:16:13,257 --> 00:16:15,857
Slap the Spaghet... スラップって
"Slap the Spaghet"... Slap means...

275
00:16:17,557 --> 00:16:18,857
叩く？
to slap?

276
00:16:21,857 --> 00:16:22,757
ん？
Huh?

277
00:16:23,257 --> 00:16:25,857
スラップってわしの思ってるスラップと一緒？
Is "slap" the same slap I'm thinking of?

278
00:16:26,557 --> 00:16:27,457
ん？
Hmm?

279
00:16:31,057 --> 00:16:33,257
英語の意味が違う？
Does it mean something different in English?

280
00:16:34,357 --> 00:16:36,257
スラップって叩く？
"Slap" means to hit, right?

281
00:16:36,557 --> 00:16:38,857
叩く以外に意味があるのじゃ？
Does it have any other meaning?

282
00:16:40,057 --> 00:16:40,957
ん？
Wait...

283
00:16:43,757 --> 00:16:45,657
調理ゲーって聞いたのじゃ。
I heard this was a cooking game.

284
00:16:46,057 --> 00:16:46,957
ん？
Huh?

285
00:16:48,357 --> 00:16:49,757
一旦進めるか。
Let's just keep going.

286
00:16:50,457 --> 00:16:55,857
えー、Slap the Spaghet by clicking the correct mouse button in the sequence.
Um, "Slap the Spaghet by clicking the correct mouse button in the sequence."

287
00:16:56,257 --> 00:16:58,457
マウスを押して操作する系か。
So you play by clicking the mouse.

288
00:16:58,657 --> 00:17:00,857
マウスのボタンを押して...
Click the mouse buttons...

289
00:17:01,157 --> 00:17:03,057
マウスのボタンってどうすんや？
How do I do the mouse buttons?

290
00:17:03,857 --> 00:17:06,657
マウスのボタンを押して、えー、操作します。
You click the mouse buttons to, um, play.

291
00:17:06,857 --> 00:17:10,857
Complete sequences to keep the Spaghet warm.

292
00:17:11,357 --> 00:17:12,157
ほう。
Oh.

293
00:17:12,557 --> 00:17:13,857
温める？
Keep it warm?

294
00:17:14,757 --> 00:17:15,657
ほう。
Hmm.

295
00:17:16,857 --> 00:17:17,757
ん？
Wait...

296
00:17:18,257 --> 00:17:20,357
これ、わしの英語合ってる？
Is my English correct here?

297
00:17:21,057 --> 00:17:23,957
なんか、スパゲッティを叩いて温めるって書いてない？
Doesn't it say to slap the spaghetti to keep it warm?

298
00:17:25,057 --> 00:17:26,457
気のせい？
Am I imagining things?

299
00:17:27,757 --> 00:17:29,357
摩擦的な？
Like friction?

300
00:17:29,457 --> 00:17:31,757
人間ってそういう能力があるのじゃ？
Do humans have that kind of ability?

301
00:17:32,157 --> 00:17:37,457
え、人間、人間って手でさ、パスタ叩いたら温められるの？わしそれ知らない！
Wait, humans can warm up pasta just by slapping it with their hands?! I didn't know that!

302
00:17:37,757 --> 00:17:40,457
サラマンダーそれ出来ないのじゃ！
Salamanders can't do that!

303
00:17:41,357 --> 00:17:44,757
え、人間って結構万能なのでは？
Wait, aren't humans pretty all-powerful then?

304
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:48,857
Complete sequences to keep the Spaghet warm.

305
00:17:48,957 --> 00:17:51,557
Try to complete the first sequence.

306
00:17:52,357 --> 00:17:53,357
ほう。
I see.

307
00:17:53,857 --> 00:17:54,857
ん？
Hmm?

308
00:17:55,357 --> 00:17:57,657
これは、レフト、ライト、レフトか？
Is this Left, Right, Left?

309
00:17:58,057 --> 00:18:01,357
SLAPって出てくるけど... SLAPって出てくるけど！
It literally says SLAP... It really says SLAP!

310
00:18:02,057 --> 00:18:03,057
え？
Huh?

311
00:18:05,757 --> 00:18:07,457
「ボヨン」言うたよ。
It made a "boing" sound.

312
00:18:07,857 --> 00:18:09,857
「ボヨン」言うたのじゃ。
It just went "boing"!

313
00:18:10,057 --> 00:18:11,357
何これ？
What is this?

314
00:18:11,557 --> 00:18:13,057
どういこっ... ん？
What does this... huh?

315
00:18:13,257 --> 00:18:15,257
これで温まるのじゃ？
This warms it up?

316
00:18:15,857 --> 00:18:17,357
こっ... ん？
Th-... huh?

317
00:18:17,857 --> 00:18:20,057
一旦チュートリアルやるか。
Let's just do the tutorial.

318
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:21,057
え、L？
Uh, L?

319
00:18:22,057 --> 00:18:24,457
手、汚れちゃうよ...
Your hands will get dirty...

320
00:18:25,057 --> 00:18:27,457
人間はこういうのができるのじゃ？
Humans can really do stuff like this?

321
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:30,057
熱エネルギー的な？
Like thermal energy?

322
00:18:30,857 --> 00:18:32,057
のじゃ？
Right?

323
00:18:36,557 --> 00:18:40,457
なんか、左上に、寒いマークと熱いマークがある。
There's a cold icon and a hot icon in the top left.

324
00:18:40,757 --> 00:18:43,257
これで温めてることになるのじゃ？
Does this count as warming it up?

325
00:18:43,857 --> 00:18:44,857
ほう。
Oh.

326
00:18:45,357 --> 00:18:50,057
Each completed sequence increases the Temperature Meter above.

327
00:18:50,257 --> 00:18:55,357
あ、左上の温度が、叩くと温度が上がるらしい。
Ah, the temperature in the top left goes up when you slap it, apparently.

328
00:18:55,757 --> 00:18:57,757
温めるってそういうこと？
That's what it means by warming it up?

329
00:18:58,257 --> 00:19:00,657
レンチンとかじゃないのじゃ？
Not like microwaving it?

330
00:19:03,057 --> 00:19:05,357
レンチンは最近の話なのじゃ？
Is microwaving a recent invention?

331
00:19:05,757 --> 00:19:09,157
この時代は手で温めてたのじゃ？
In this era, did they warm it up by hand?

332
00:19:09,757 --> 00:19:13,557
If the Temperature Meter gets too low...

333
00:19:13,857 --> 00:19:16,857
温度が低くなってしまったら、
If the temperature gets too low,

334
00:19:17,057 --> 00:19:19,457
the Spaghet will freeze?!

335
00:19:21,357 --> 00:19:23,557
スパゲッティ凍っちゃうらしい！
Apparently the spaghetti will freeze!

336
00:19:24,057 --> 00:19:25,257
みんなそうしてる？
Does everyone do this?

337
00:19:25,357 --> 00:19:27,057
あ、みんなそうしてるんだ...
Ah, everyone does this...

338
00:19:27,157 --> 00:19:28,257
知らなかった。
I had no idea.

339
00:19:28,357 --> 00:19:29,857
「レンチンが古い」？レンジが古い？！
"Microwaves are old"? Microwaves are old?!

340
00:19:30,057 --> 00:19:32,257
でも手汚れちゃうよ、むしろ！
But your hands will get dirty instead!

341
00:19:32,857 --> 00:19:36,057
ほう... え、でも、ホラーゲームだから、
I see... But wait, since it's a horror game,

342
00:19:36,357 --> 00:19:38,257
なんか、温めないと、
if you don't warm it up,

343
00:19:38,757 --> 00:19:42,557
この左上のメーターが一番左に行っちゃうと、
and that meter in the top left reaches the far left,

344
00:19:42,857 --> 00:19:44,857
パスタが冷めちゃって、
the pasta will cool down,

345
00:19:45,057 --> 00:19:46,857
凍っちゃうらしい。凍るって何？
and freeze, apparently. Wait, freeze?!

346
00:19:47,857 --> 00:19:51,557
氷ってそんな簡単に作っていいのじゃ？
Can ice really be made that easily?!

347
00:19:52,057 --> 00:19:53,657
If that happens...

348
00:19:53,857 --> 00:19:55,257
its all over...

349
00:19:55,357 --> 00:19:57,457
全てが終わりだって！どういうこと？！
It says it's all over! What does that mean?!

350
00:19:57,557 --> 00:19:59,057
本気すぎじゃろ！
Taking it way too seriously!

351
00:19:59,157 --> 00:20:00,057
パスタの温めに。
Over warming up pasta!

352
00:20:00,469 --> 00:20:03,069
"Press [A] to continue" のじゃ?
"Press [A] to continue", right?

353
00:20:04,869 --> 00:20:07,069
なんか思ってたのと違うのじゃ。
This is kinda different from what I expected.

354
00:20:07,069 --> 00:20:11,869
なんか クッキングゲームみたいな クッキングシミュレーター的なのを想像してきたのじゃ。
I imagined something like a cooking game, a Cooking Simulator-style game.

355
00:20:12,469 --> 00:20:16,869
なんか 湯切りして パスタを何分茹でて湯切りして
Like draining the pasta, boiling it for a few minutes, straining it...

356
00:20:16,869 --> 00:20:21,569
あのソースかけて 客に提供するみたいな。
...pouring sauce on it, and serving it to customers.

357
00:20:22,069 --> 00:20:26,069
え? ゲームってさ そういうの あるよね?
Wait, games like that exist, right?

358
00:20:26,069 --> 00:20:29,069
なんか パスタシミュレーターみたいな。
Like a pasta simulator or something.

359
00:20:29,569 --> 00:20:30,869
のじゃ?
Right?

360
00:20:31,069 --> 00:20:33,069
Let's cooking?

361
00:20:34,869 --> 00:20:37,569
人間はこれが普通なのじゃ?
Is this normal for humans?

362
00:20:38,269 --> 00:20:41,069
人間は こういうのが...
Do humans...

363
00:20:41,069 --> 00:20:42,869
好きなの?!
...like this kind of thing?!

364
00:20:43,069 --> 00:20:44,269
ええ...
Well...

365
00:20:44,269 --> 00:20:49,069
はい。"If you click the incorrect mouse"... 間違ったマウス押してしまうと マウスボタン押してしまうと
Alright. "If you click the incorrect mouse..." If you click the wrong mouse, the wrong mouse button...

366
00:20:49,069 --> 00:20:52,269
"you'll punch the Spaghet." ほう。
..."you'll punch the Spaghet." Oho.

367
00:20:52,269 --> 00:20:55,869
ああ これはあれかな? あの ゲーム性じゃ。
Ah, is this what they call gameplay mechanics?

368
00:20:55,869 --> 00:21:02,069
なるほど。間違ったボタン押しちゃうと 叩くじゃなくて殴るになってしまうらしいのじゃ。
I see. If you press the wrong button, it turns into punching instead of slapping.

369
00:21:02,269 --> 00:21:05,869
"This will cause the temperature to drop faster." あ
"This will cause the temperature to drop faster." Ah...

370
00:21:06,069 --> 00:21:10,569
殴ると ホントは叩かなきゃいけないのを殴ってしまうと
If you punch it, if you punch it instead of slapping it...

371
00:21:10,569 --> 00:21:14,869
温度が急激に落ちてしまって 冷えやすくなっちゃうのかな?
...the temperature drops rapidly and it cools down faster, maybe?

372
00:21:15,069 --> 00:21:17,569
"Complete the next 4 sequences."

373
00:21:17,869 --> 00:21:20,269
ええ ライト ライト ライト。
Let's see: right, right, right.

374
00:21:20,569 --> 00:21:22,569
な 何これ?
Wh-What is this?

375
00:21:22,569 --> 00:21:27,569
ぺちょんぺちょん言ってる... ぺ ぺ ぺちょんぺちょん言ってるけど。
It's making squishy sounds... Squish, squish, it's making squishy sounds.

376
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:30,469
ぺちょん ぺちょんぺちょん言ってるけど。
Squish, squish, squishing sounds.

377
00:21:30,469 --> 00:21:32,469
音ゲーなのじゃ?
Is this a rhythm game?

378
00:21:32,569 --> 00:21:34,569
音ゲーなのじゃ?
Is this a rhythm game?

379
00:21:34,869 --> 00:21:36,069
ん?
Hm?

380
00:21:36,869 --> 00:21:42,569
"In the top right corner of the screen, there is a Visibility Meter."

381
00:21:42,569 --> 00:21:44,869
なんかあるよね 右にな。
There is something on the right, yeah.

382
00:21:44,869 --> 00:21:51,569
"This meter fills whenever an unwanted spectator watches you." どういうこと?
"This meter fills whenever an unwanted spectator watches you." What does that mean?

383
00:21:51,569 --> 00:21:54,069
何が見てるの?
What is watching?

384
00:21:54,069 --> 00:21:58,869
"If the meter fills completely, you lose." 負けます。
"If the meter fills completely, you lose." You lose.

385
00:21:58,869 --> 00:22:00,369
何?!
What?!

386
00:22:00,369 --> 00:22:03,569
調理ゲーと聞いている! 調理ゲーと聞いていますのじゃ!
I was told this was a cooking game! I was told it's a cooking game!

387
00:22:04,069 --> 00:22:07,569
調理ゲーかと思ったら音ゲーじゃし
I thought it was a cooking game, but it's a rhythm game, and...

388
00:22:07,869 --> 00:22:10,569
ホラーゲー?! これが?!
A horror game?! This is?!

389
00:22:11,069 --> 00:22:16,269
競合なのじゃ? 自社コンテンツの競合コンテンツですのじゃ?
Is this competition? A rival to our company's content?

390
00:22:16,569 --> 00:22:20,069
それを回してるのじゃ? それはいいの?
And I'm streaming it? Is that really okay?

391
00:22:20,869 --> 00:22:26,569
え "Let's avoid that. Look down at the arrow."
Uh, "Let's avoid that. Look down at the arrow."

392
00:22:27,069 --> 00:22:32,069
"Left Click when you see HIDE to crouch behind the counter." あ
"Left Click when you see HIDE to crouch behind the counter." Ah...

393
00:22:32,069 --> 00:22:35,069
隠れられるんだ。
...so you can hide.

394
00:22:35,069 --> 00:22:37,569
何が見てるの わしを?
What is watching me?

395
00:22:37,569 --> 00:22:39,569
何が見てるの?
What's watching?

396
00:22:39,569 --> 00:22:46,569
なんか 何かがわしのことを見てるっぽくて なんか隠れたりもできるらしいけど...
Apparently something is watching me, and I can hide from it too, but...

397
00:22:47,069 --> 00:22:50,069
"Left Click when you see HIDE"... HIDE どうやってやるんじゃ?
"Left Click when you see HIDE"... How do I hide?

398
00:22:50,069 --> 00:22:52,269
ちょ 今んとこない。
Wait, there's nothing right now.

399
00:22:52,269 --> 00:22:54,669
今んとこなさそう。
Doesn't seem to be anything right now.

400
00:22:55,069 --> 00:22:56,269
あ あった。
Ah, there it is!

401
00:22:56,269 --> 00:23:00,069
なるほど。下に行くとHIDE 下に行くと隠れられるっぽい。
I see. Looking down gives HIDE. Looking down lets me hide.

402
00:23:00,069 --> 00:23:03,069
誰から隠れてるのじゃ?
Who am I hiding from?

403
00:23:03,069 --> 00:23:09,569
え "While down here, you can't be seen by anyone on the other side of the counter."
Uh, "While down here, you can't be seen by anyone on the other side of the counter."

404
00:23:09,569 --> 00:23:15,069
向こう側にいる人の誰からも見られなくなります ここに隠れてるからね。
No one on the other side can see you, because you're hiding here, right?

405
00:23:15,069 --> 00:23:22,069
"Keep in mind that you are still exposed on your side. Press [A] to continue." ほう。
"Keep in mind that you are still exposed on your side. Press [A] to continue." I see.

406
00:23:23,069 --> 00:23:24,869
どういうこと?
What does that mean?

407
00:23:25,069 --> 00:23:27,869
これ な 何 何をするゲームなのじゃ?
Wh-What kind of game is this?

408
00:23:27,869 --> 00:23:35,869
"To stand, look up at the arrow on the edge of the counter. Left Click when you see STAND UP." オッケー。スタンドアップ?
"To stand, look up at the arrow on the edge of the counter. Left Click when you see STAND UP." Okay. Stand up?

409
00:23:37,869 --> 00:23:40,069
ほう ほう ほう。
Right, right, right.

410
00:23:40,069 --> 00:23:47,569
"In the event that there is a threat on this side of the counter, you'll need to hide..."

411
00:23:47,869 --> 00:23:49,869
なるほど?
I see?

412
00:23:50,069 --> 00:23:53,069
また別のとこに隠れる必要もあるらしい。
Apparently I need to hide somewhere else too.

413
00:23:53,069 --> 00:24:00,069
"To do so, look at the arrow ahead of you, on the opposite side of the counter." 逆側にも隠れられますよと。
"To do so, look at the arrow ahead of you, on the opposite side of the counter." You can hide on the opposite side too.

414
00:24:00,569 --> 00:24:02,069
"JUMP ACROSS"?

415
00:24:02,069 --> 00:24:03,569
ジャンプアクロス?!
Jump across?!

416
00:24:03,569 --> 00:24:06,069
飛んで逃げられるのじゃ?!
You can jump and run away?!

417
00:24:06,069 --> 00:24:07,569
ほう。
Oho.

418
00:24:07,569 --> 00:24:10,069
"Try it out." 試せ。
"Try it out." Give it a try.

419
00:24:10,069 --> 00:24:17,569
"To return from that side, look up at the arrow on the edge of the counter, and Left Click when you see JUMP BACK."

420
00:24:17,569 --> 00:24:23,069
"Press [A] when you're back behind the original side of the counter to continue."

421
00:24:24,069 --> 00:24:27,569
ん? 何から隠れてるの?
Hm? What am I hiding from?

422
00:24:28,069 --> 00:24:32,069
なんか 逃げ 逃げ要素ありということ?
Wait, does that mean there's an evasion element?

423
00:24:32,069 --> 00:24:33,269
ほう。
Oho.

424
00:24:33,269 --> 00:24:36,069
逃げ要素あり? ほう。
An evasion element? I see.

425
00:24:36,069 --> 00:24:38,069
アクションゲーム?
An action game?

426
00:24:38,069 --> 00:24:39,569
ほう。
Oho.

427
00:24:40,569 --> 00:24:42,569
まあ やってみるか。
Well, let's try it out.

428
00:24:42,569 --> 00:24:46,069
はい。"This concludes the tutorial."
Alright. "This concludes the tutorial."

429
00:24:46,069 --> 00:24:52,569
"To view this information again, you can enable it in the Settings menu. Press [A] to close."

430
00:24:52,869 --> 00:24:56,569
はい。まあ 大体 大体分かったのじゃ。
Alright. Well, I basically get it.

431
00:24:56,569 --> 00:24:59,869
大体言いたいことは分かった。
I get the general idea of what it's saying.

432
00:25:01,081 --> 00:25:01,781
うん
Yeah.

433
00:25:03,381 --> 00:25:04,781
やってみるか
Let's give it a try.

434
00:25:05,981 --> 00:25:07,481
ジャンプ アクロス
"Jump across."

435
00:25:10,581 --> 00:25:11,881
何？何？何？
What? What? What?

436
00:25:11,881 --> 00:25:13,181
何何何何？！
What, what, what, what?!

437
00:25:13,181 --> 00:25:14,581
何が起きた？何が起きた？
What happened?! What happened?!

438
00:25:14,581 --> 00:25:15,881
何？何？何？
What? What? What?

439
00:25:15,881 --> 00:25:17,281
待って、何？何？
Wait, what? What?

440
00:25:17,281 --> 00:25:18,981
なんかすごい音する！
There's a crazy sound!

441
00:25:18,981 --> 00:25:20,581
え、絶対動いちゃダメな…何？な、ちょっ…
Wait, am I definitely not supposed to move...? What? W-wait...

442
